# Omelo employer portal — environment variables.
# Copy to .env.local for development. Every variable the app reads is listed here.
#
# Only the Supabase PUBLISHABLE key belongs in this app. It is safe in a browser
# bundle by design: every access decision is made by RLS in the database.
# The SERVICE ROLE key must never appear in this file, this app, or its host's
# environment settings.

# Supabase project URL (Settings -> API). Used by the browser client, the server
# client, the proxy (session refresh), the auth-signup Edge Function call and
# the Omelo Meet leave beacon. Also the origin for Realtime websockets (wss).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co

# Supabase publishable key (sb_publishable_...). Sent as the apikey on every
# request; the signed-in user's session supplies identity.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_xxx

# Not read by this app: the LiveKit server URL for Omelo Meet is returned by the
# meet-token Edge Function at join time, and LiveKit secrets live only in
# Supabase Edge Function secrets.

# Optional: error reporting. When set, src/lib/observability.ts sends errors
# from error boundaries and server actions to Sentry's envelope endpoint (no SDK).
# When unset, errors are only logged to the console. This is a public DSN
# (safe in the browser bundle). If a Content-Security-Policy is added, allow
# its host in connect-src.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://<public_key>@o<org>.ingest.sentry.io/<project_id>
